    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/48868b2ecf269e286a4eda6c38fcf72bf4b68054ad8c565ce0e2286917f3f6ef.png)\n\nThe curve $y=f(x)$ is shown above. At which of the following points is $f(x)$ continuous?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=3$\n- **II.** $x=6$\n- **III.** $x=8$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's consider each point separately.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=3.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=3$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=6.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=6$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=8.$ Since there is an asymptote at $x=8,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=8$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is  \"I and II only\".\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/7dc9ad6ca93592b22886830abebc6f204f0b0319dd4ae723aa3f86cc4a9d2d24.png)",
