  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186068695,
      "id": "6cd6c125-ecaf-5847-a802-ec1b3594a15c",
      "title": "Determining Whether a Function Is Continuous at a Given Point"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/5f4cddb0cc120e2a267367ca43f1c2a3e339ffabfebf10342ca0c7c7cfc70cca.png)\n\nThe curve $y=f(x)$ is shown above. At which of the following points is $f(x)$ continuous?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=-17$\n- **II.** $x=-11$\n- **III.** $x=-5$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's consider each point separately.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-17.$ Because there is a jump at $x=-17,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=-17$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-11.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=-11$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-5.$ Since there is a break at $x=-5,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=-5$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is: \"II only\".",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
